{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Importance of HTML "}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about the importance of HTML. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Represent the solution outline to the problem presented by the customer through making case of use diagrams, facing the problem to the customer following rules and protocols of the organization."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Writes simple and short texts about programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Present Tense Statements with When to Talk about Facts"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">when</span> to express what people generally do in certain situations. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "By using <span class=\"strong\">when</span>, you can describe a situation; we usually divide that situation into two clauses, one with <span class=\"strong\">when</span>and the other one with the result or consequence of that specific situation.  Let's take a look at the following structures to create statements using <span class=\"strong\">when</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">When</span> + Statement in Simple Present, + Result or Consequence in Simple Present</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">When </span> you know the rules of tags, it's really simple to create an HTML page. </span><br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, it is possible to change the order of the clauses: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Result or Consequence in Simple Present + <span class=\"strong\">When</span> + Statement in Simple Present</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\">It's really simple to create an HTML page <span class=\"strong\">when</span> you know the rules of tags. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "\tWhen you don't have HTML in a page, there is no essential content, so you basically don't have a web page. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "\tHTML is a markup language; when we use it, it allows us to display different multimedia content on a website and provides users with hyperlinks to access different pages."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you add angle brackets to certain codes, you transform a regular text into a page component."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "How to Summarize an Article"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Summarizing is taking up the details of a document in order to give a brief explanation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In order to sum up an article, you should consider the following steps: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>First, scan and highlight main ideas and key words in the article.</li> <li>Read the article carefully. While reading, take notes of the remarkable ideas you find by using your own words. </li> <li>Do not rephrase the same article words or sentences since your summary can probably seem plagiarized. </li> <li>Once you have an outline of the main facts of your article, start writing your summary using the ideas you wrote before. </li> <li>Organize your text in paragraphs. The first paragraph should be an introduction where you state the relationship between the article and your text. Then, you need to provide supporting details about the topic keeping an objective point of view; finally, you need to give a conclusion according to the information provided in the article. </li> <li>Do not forget to mention bibliographical information such as the authors' full name. </li> <li> Avoid quoting directly from the article. </li> <li>Remember not to include any personal opinion or point of view. </li> <li>The length of your text should be shorter than the original. </li> <li>Once you finish, proofread your summary. </li> </ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "backbone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an essential part of a structure"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is necessary to keep in mind that only HTML can be considered as the backbone of a web page."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "page behavior "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "refers to all the actions or operations on a web page "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: HTML is in charge of the page structure which is far more important than controlling the page design or the page behavior."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "markup language "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a type of coding that uses tags to add web features to normal text  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: HTML is a markup language; when we use it, it allows us to display different multimedia content on a website and provides users with hyperlinks to access different pages."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hyperlink"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a mechanism that connects a page or document with another one by clicking on it "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: HTML is a markup language; when we use it, it allows us to display different multimedia content on a website and provides users with hyperlinks to access different pages. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strength"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an advantage or positive point of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The greatest strength of HTML is its simplicity, HTML syntax can be really easy to learn and accessible to different kinds of public, not only programmers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trademark"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a symbol or mark that identifies something in particular "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The trademarks of HTML are tags; when you add angle brackets to certain codes, you transform a regular text into a page component."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob12aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for an article about the most recent usages and updates for HTLM"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Get the main information of the text."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Organize the information in a Venn diagram. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain to your classmates the most recent usages and updates for HTML."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about the most recent usages and updates for HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I get the main idea of the text. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I organize the information by using a Venn diagram. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain to my partners the most recent usages and updates for HTML. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le03ob12re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"strong\">Why is HTML important?\n</span></div><br>\nWeb developers know that the most significant languages to design websites and web content are HTML, CCS, and JavaScript. However, it is necessary to keep in mind that only HTML can be considered as the backbone of a web page. <br>\nWhy is HTML more important than the other languages? Well, the answer is simple. HTML is in charge of the page structure which is far more important than controlling the page design or the page behavior as CSS or JavaScript respectively do; when you don't have HTML in a page, there is no essential content, so you basically don't have a web page."}, {"time": "46000", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "HTML is a markup language; when we use it, it allows us to display different multimedia content on a website and provides users with hyperlinks to access different pages. Thus, what HTML basically does is to mark content with tags to definite features and establish relationships among different types of content in a website. <br>\nThe greatest strength of HTML is its simplicity, HTML syntax can be really easy to learn and accessible to different kinds of public, not only programmers. The trademarks of HTML are tags; when you add angle brackets to certain codes, you transform a regular text into a page component. For example, if you use angle brackets for the letter b, it becomes a tag that makes a regular text bold."}, {"time": "103000", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "To sum up, we can say that HTML defines the internet itself. HTML makes it possible to display and interact with different types of online contents, and because of its simplicity, it can be really easy for you to learn how to use it very quickly; of course, HTML has some other aspects that are more complex, however, with dedication, you can become an expert."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le03ob12re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can understand written information about the importance of HTML for web design. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss the importance of HTML tags in webpages. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can summarize information from a text."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What happens if we take away the HTML from a web page?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think working with HTML is easy? Why? Why not?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "The Essential Structure for Web Pages"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "ques